# A triple-backtick fenced block dedents its interior to the fence's column,
# ignores the leading and trailing newline, and still does {curly} substitution
# with multi-line literal text merged into a single argument.

# Simple fenced block: one line of content, dedented flush.
say ```
    Hello, world.
    ```

# Fenced block with a blank line and a {curly} substitution: the literal text
# around the curly stays one continuous argument across the line breaks.
say ```
    Hello.

    {name}
    ```

$ facts
$ assert parse say (`) (Hello, world.) (`)
$ assert parse say (`) (Hello.

) { name } (`)